    "IFT6": "ift_terminal_descent/ift6_ship_last600s_2hz.csv",
    "reduction": "last 600 s of each video at 2 Hz, Starship corrected altitude and speed columns only; time is video time (frame/30), not mission elapsed time"
  },
  "analysis_script": "scripts/ift_terminal_descent.py",
  "assumptions_and_limits": [
    "Displayed altitude has 1 km resolution; each k -> k-1 km change is taken at k-0.5 km. A 0.5 km datum error shifts the ratio by about 5 %.",
    "Displayed speed is total speed (frame unstated); it is treated as vertical. The glide component is small near 90 deg angle of attack, but it biases the ratio up by about (1 + (v_h/v)^2).",
    "Steady terminal fall (drag = weight) is assumed between 12 and 2 km. Above about 8 km the ship still decelerates, which biases the ratio low there.",
    "Density from the U.S. Standard Atmosphere 1976 troposphere, not the day's weather; this is a few percent.",
    "OCR artefacts are possible; the extractor fills gaps and removes outliers automatically.",
    "The ratio is m/(C_D S) for the whole vehicle at its flown attitude and flap setting; mass is unknown."
  ],
